    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1011">

                <pb facs="1054" n="1040" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1040"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.01/98: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Scotten</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-01T12:00:00-05:00">June 1,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>544. I will send my recommendations later on today regarding the general question
                    of recognition of the new government. However, prior to any determination I
                    would appreciate the Department’s immediate instructions whether I should
                    establish an informal contact either with the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs<anchor n="11" xml:id="d1011-f1"/> or with Velasco Ibarra or whether,
                    in case they desire to see me, I should go.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1011-f1" n="11" xml:id="d1011-f1-content">
                <p>Camilo Ponce Enríquez.</p>
            </note>
